      "representation": "recall",
      "questionType": "short_answer",
      "prompt": "给定新句子（假设适用本课规则）：主动句 'The mechanic repairs the car.' 及其相应被动句 'The car is repaired by the mechanic.' 请识别：1) 主动句中动作的施事、动作、受事分别是什么；2) 被动句的语法主语是什么，它是施事还是受事，实际动作执行者是谁？",
      "rubric": [
        {
          "id": "criterion_892d415a-9859-4a1f-a78d-2528b74d051d",
          "text": "正确指出主动句施事为the mechanic、动作为repairs、受事为the car",
          "required": true,
          "sourceBindingIds": [
            "blk_0_1c59de98"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "criterion_1102e1d9-208a-40c5-be42-171d2a7f57b8",
          "text": "正确指出被动句语法主语为the car且为受事（非施事），实际执行者是the mechanic",
          "required": true,
          "sourceBindingIds": [
            "blk_0_1c59de98"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourceBindings": [
        {
          "materialId": "mat_13a97d5a-fea5-464d-a807-06b5c9bf0cea",
          "materialRevisionId": "rev_c84b5b67-3266-4765-8bea-97adcb08af07",
          "sourceBlockId": "blk_0_1c59de98",
          "quote": "英语主动句通常把动作的施事放在主语位置，如“The editor checks the report.”编辑是检查动作的执行者，报告是受到检查的对象。相应被动句为“The report is checked by the editor.”报告成为语法主语，但它仍是动作的受事，并没有变成检查别人的执行者。改变语态可以改变叙述重点，而不必改变所报告的事件。",
          "contentOrigin": "extracted_original",
          "authoritative": true
        }
      ],
      "formalEligible": true,
      "policyReason": "FORMAL_ELIGIBLE"
    }
